      <section class="challenge-section section-pad" id="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow section-label"><span>04 /</span> Challenge process</p>
              <h2 id="process-title">From a question<br />to an outcome.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>An illustrative twelve-week cycle. Each actual timeline depends on the complexity, the institution's capacity, data readiness, and any research or ethics approvals.</p>
          </div>
          <ol class="challenge-timeline">
            <li><span class="challenge-time">Weeks 1–2</span><div><h3>Scope together</h3><p>Institution and SciStitch agree on the problem, stakeholders, evidence, open licensing, data permissions, evaluation criteria, and a named validation contact.</p></div></li>
            <li><span class="challenge-time">Weeks 3–4</span><div><h3>Form the team</h3><p>Invite relevant collaborators, define contributions, discuss research methods, and confirm review milestones and responsibilities.</p></div></li>
            <li><span class="challenge-time">Weeks 5–8</span><div><h3>Research and develop</h3><p>Investigate, analyze, and build with regular institutional feedback; document assumptions and limitations.</p></div></li>
            <li><span class="challenge-time">Weeks 9–10</span><div><h3>Validate and review</h3><p>Review scientific and technical quality, reproducibility, and usefulness together with the institution.</p></div></li>
            <li><span class="challenge-time">Weeks 11–12</span><div><h3>Release or document</h3><p>Share the approved, openly licensed outcomes with clear contributor credit; agree on handover or separately funded follow-up.</p></div></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
